license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  QSOL NEXUS 2.1.1 is the release-candidate line for the post-v2.0 extension
  surface: LATTICE-backed world presence, default-deny admitted instruments,
  typed persistent-world relations/hypotheses/experiments and quarantined
  exchange, secure remote-operator setup, and the completed Three Minds, One
  World integration. It preserves the equal-vote Council, content-addressed
  WorldStore/Ark continuity, reviewed local and fixed-host model adapters,
  defensive/civic/culture boundaries, and the rule that provider identity,
  persistence, instrument output, geometry, consensus, and social history do
  not create additional epistemic or governance authority. Cite the tagged
  release applicable to the software actually used; the historical v2.1.0 tag
  is not moved by the v2.1.1 release process.
keywords:
  - cognitive substrate
  - AI council
  - multi-model systems
  - model interoperability
  - persistent world
  - provenance
  - reproducible research
  - human-AI collaboration
  - formal verification
